  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian government is currently managing significant updates to teacher staffing policies during the National Teacher Day observation period. Amidst the announcement of 154,052 civil servant (CPNS) formations for 2026, legislative bodies such as House Commission X are calling for clearer implementation guidelines, particularly regarding the 35-year age limit for applicants transitioning from part-time PPPK positions. Local administrations are simultaneously responding to national directives by upgrading teacher employment status. For instance, the Majalengka regency government confirmed the transition of part-time PPPK teachers to full-time roles starting January 2027, with funding provided by the Ministry of Primary and Secondary Education. Similarly, leadership in East Kalimantan has prioritized the conversion of part-time teachers to full-time staff, while the West Nusa Tenggara administration has issued financial incentives to support thousands of current educators.",
